;; spec:   stdlib §2.7 (pr-str is Debug), §4.3 (row print-method: the type needs both instances), §4.14 (row pr-str)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Debug for Pt
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: pr-str
;; The twin of `pr` asks Debug and nothing else, so a type that defined only `impl Show` (what `println`
;; prints) is refused when the program is checked, with the checker's own words: the twin adds no message
;; of its own and hides none. Used as a value, in `(map pr-str ps)`, it is the same refusal, because the
;; twin is one generic function monomorphised at `Pt`. A user type that wants both `println` and `pr`
;; defines both instances (case 2955).
(ns main)

(defstruct Pt (x: i64 y: i64))
(impl Show Pt (show (self) "Pt"))

(defun main () -> i64 (count (map pr-str [(Pt 1 2)])))
